# No private key material belongs in this repository.
#
# Everything below is produced by generate-certificates.sh, which Gradle runs
# automatically before any test that needs it. Regenerating mints fresh CA
# keypairs, so the public certificates and truststores derived from them are
# generated too - committing them would leave a fresh clone with trust anchors
# that do not match its own keys.
#
# Tracked here: generate-certificates.sh, README.md, the .ext openssl configs,
# and public_ca/public-roots.p12 (real third-party roots, public entries only,
# not derived from any key we generate).

*.p12
*.cer
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.csr
*.srl

# Public roots are not generated - they are real third-party certificates and
# contain no private key. See README.md for the refresh procedure.
!public_ca/public-roots.p12
